# LOCAL run (2026-11-08). After an independent review of the SAC setup, the user chose
# to remove "Pre-tanh penalty + PER" and to apply "Uniform transitions (fix sampler)".
# This is the rs10 run (slurm/local_c0ft_t05_sac_rs10.env: c0 fine-tuned on Town05 with
# rewards x10 in the environment, no value clips, plain SAC actor loss alpha*logpi - Q,
# learned log-std, auto-tuned temperature) plus:
#   * ACTOR_PRETANH_L2=0: no penalty on the actor's pre-tanh mean. It was set by
#     v16_overlay.env (0.1, free 1.5); neither SAC nor REDQ has it.
#   * PER_ALPHA=0: uniform replay, not prioritised.
#   * UNIFORM_TRANSITIONS=1: every stored transition is trained equally often. The old
#     sampler trained an episode's first CHUNK_T - 1 = 39 rows, and all of a short
#     episode, less: up to a 25x spread across transitions on a mixed test replay.
#   * GOAL_BATCH_FRAC=none: no forced 50/50 goal/explore batches. Each mode's share of
#     a batch is its share of the replay.
# Still in place: c0's demos pinned in the replay with the arrival approach cut, never
# moving the temperature; c0's encoder and GRU frozen; LayerNorm critics; HER; critic
# warm-up (5000 updates) and actor freeze (5000 online updates); 15% noise-free
# episodes; 100-step stall truncation; the junction curriculum. These were kept either
# by the user's rules or by the user's choice when shown the review's list.
. "$REPO/slurm/local_c0ft_t05_sac_rs10.env"
# The four settings above, and every other plain-SAC one (user rule 2026-11-08), come
# from the canonical file, sourced last. In effect it is the same run launched at 20:58
# from 95cc63e, which exported ACTOR_PRETANH_L2=0 PER_ALPHA=0 UNIFORM_TRANSITIONS=1
# GOAL_BATCH_FRAC=none here; the rest already held.
. "$REPO/slurm/plain_sac.env"
